v.log` becomes `grav.log.1`, older copies are gzipped (`grav.log.2.gz` and on), and five are kept. `grav.log`, `security.log` and `scheduler.log` rotate as they are written, an hourly `log-rotate` scheduler job catches plugin logs, and `bin/grav logrotate` runs it by hand. Change or turn it off under `system.log.rotate` (Configuration → System → Error handler)\n- A page can unpublish everything below it along with itself. Set `cascade_unpublish: true` on a page (Options → \"Unpublish child pages too\"), and while that page is unpublished, by `published: false` or by its `publish_date` / `unpublish_date`, every page below it is unpublished too: left out of menus, collections, the sitemap and search, and not served. The pages below keep their own `published` setting, so they are back as they were once the parent is published again, and a section given a `publish_date` goes live all at once. `system.pages.cascade_unpublish` (Configuration → System → Content) sets the default for every page, and is off. `$page->unpublishedBy()` returns the route of the page that hides a page\n\n### Bugfix\n- A backup profile's Scheduled Backup switch now decides on its own whether the backup runs. An old Enabled or Disabled entry for the backup job in `user/config/scheduler.yaml`, which classic admin wrote whenever its Scheduler page was saved, used to override it, so backups could stop with the switch on [#4397](https://github.com/getgrav/grav/issues/4397)\n- A scheduler job that fails now keeps what it printed to standard output as well as its error output, so the reason shows in the job's history, `user/data/scheduler/status.yaml` and the output file. Most console commands print their errors to standard output, so a failed run used to be recorded with no output at all\n- A page with a link or image whose address is longer than any file path, such as an inline image written as `/data:image/png;base64,...`, no longer turns into an error page on servers with `open_basedir` set\n- Several Grav sites on one server no longer try to load each other's files. The class loader's APCu cache is now kept separate for each site, so a class found in one site's `vendor/` folder is never looked up at another site's path [#4392](https://github.com/getgrav/grav/issues/4392)\n- The Page IDs option and the GFM and table Markdown options in Configuration → System use translation keys instead of English written into the blueprint, so they can be translated. The English comes from Admin2 2.2.13 and Admin 1.10.63","upstream_url":"https://github.com/getgrav/grav/releases/tag/2.2.29"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/root","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR=:/config/php","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true"],"exposed_ports":["443/tcp","80/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/layers.amd64.json","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/layers.arm64.json"},"packages":{},"release":"https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-grav/releases/tag/2.2.29-ls13","pages":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/","files":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/files.amd64.json.gz","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/files.arm64.json.gz"},"sbom":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-grav/builds/2.2.29-ls13/packages.amd64.json.gz","arm64":